# Homepage

Lead with what the household does most, and keep current conditions apart from navigation. A homepage prioritises a few routes rather than linking to everything. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

For a Home Assistant Overview, put useful household status and frequent tasks first. Use familiar room and domain names, with a visible label beside each meaningful native icon. The documentation homepage instead introduces the design system and its main learning routes.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a concise heading, a small number of task links and grouped secondary routes. Follow the local action-links component for navigational arrows. Let whitespace and headings do most of the grouping, and do not put a heavy card border round every destination. Repeated icons must keep one meaning ([WG-081](../../content/formatting-content/text-formatting.html#wg-081)).

## Home Assistant boundary

A household homepage is not a copy of www.gov.uk. Use the household's chosen name and any artwork it is authorised to use, never the crown or an official masthead. Priorities depend on the household, so do not assume a universal "most used" task. Do not show invented readings, and show an unavailable reading as unavailable ([WG-033](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-033)).

